      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We assessed the relation between the circumferential distribution of coronary atherosclerotic plaques and the structure of the epicardial coronary arteries in patients with coronary artery disease using intravascular ultrasound in vivo. Coronary atherosclerosis preferentially formed at the inner arc of the curved coronary vessels, and greater vessel curvatures were associated with greater distributions of atherosclerotic lesions along the inner coronary artery wall."},
